52 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 44 0 R
/E (The photovoltaic \(PV\) array is modeled using the single-diode equivalent circuit, which accurately represents the electrical behavior of a practical solar cell while maintaining computational simplicity. The model consists of a photocurrent source Iph, a diode, a series resistance Rs, and a shunt resistance Rp. The photocurrent source represents the current generated due to incident solar radiation, the diode models the p-n junction characteristics of the solar cell, the series resistance accounts for internal resistive losses in the semiconductor material and metallic contacts, and the shunt resistance represents leakage currents caused by imperfections within the cell. Together, these components reproduce the nonlinear current-voltage \(I-V\) characteristics of a real photovoltaic module.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
53 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 44 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
54 0 obj
