92 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 45 0 R
/E (In the Simulink implementation shown, the irradiance input is first converted into the corresponding photocurrent, which drives the controlled current source representing the generated solar current. Simultaneously, the temperature input is used to calculate the thermal voltage required in the diode equation. The diode block computes the exponential junction current, while the shunt resistance accounts for leakage losses. The output current is measured using the current sensor, and the voltage drop across the series resistance is calculated and subtracted from the internal diode voltage to obtain the terminal voltage of the PV array. Finally, the model outputs the terminal voltage Vpv, output current Ipv, diode current, and irradiance, which are subsequently supplied to the MPPT controller and the DC-DC boost converter for maximum power extraction and grid integration.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
