145 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 47 0 R
/E (The 500 V DC output from the boost converter is supplied to a three-level Voltage Source Converter \(VSC\), which converts it into a 60 Hz three-phase AC output for grid integration. Two series-connected DC-link capacitors split the input voltage equally, creating a neutral point required for three-level operation while stabilizing the DC-link voltage. The inverter generates three voltage levels +Vdc/2, 0, -Vdc/2, reducing harmonic distortion and improving output waveform quality. An L-filter is used at the inverter output to suppress switching harmonics before power is delivered to the grid.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
146 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 47 0 R
/E (Three-Level Voltage Source Converter \(VSC\))
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
