151 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 47 0 R
/T (In the implemented controller, the zero-sequence component is discarded using a Selector block because the grid-connected three-phase system operates under balanced conditions. Consequently, only the d-axis and q-axis components are supplied to the control loops. Since the PLL aligns the rotating reference frame with the grid voltage vector, the transformed d and q quantities become nearly constant under steady-state conditions. This conversion of sinusoidal three-phase signals into DC quantities significantly simplifies PI controller design and enables independent regulation of active and reactive power in the grid-connected inverter.)
/E (In the implemented controller, the zero-sequence component is discarded using a Selector block because the grid-connected three-phase system operates under balanced conditions. Consequently, only the d-axis and q-axis components are supplied to the control loops. Since the PLL aligns the rotating reference frame with the grid voltage vector, the transformed d and q quantities become nearly constant under steady-state conditions. This conversion of sinusoidal three-phase signals into DC quantities significantly simplifies PI controller design and enables independent regulation of active and reactive power in the grid-connected inverter.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
152 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 47 0 R
/E (The measured DC-link voltage is compared with its reference value in the VDC Regulator, which generates the reference d-axis current Id required to maintain a constant DC-link voltage. The q-axis current reference Iq is set to zero to achieve unity power factor operation.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
153 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 47 0 R
/E (The Current Regulator compares the reference currents with the measured currents and calculates the required converter voltage components in the dq reference frame. These voltage references are then converted back into three-phase reference voltages by the Uabc_ref Generation block using the grid angle obtained from the PLL.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
154 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 47 0 R
/E (Finally, the PWM Generator converts the three-phase reference voltages into switching pulses, which are applied to the Voltage Source Converter \(VSC\). These pulses control the inverter to inject the desired power into the grid while maintaining the DC-link voltage at its reference value.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
