/Title (In the implemented controller, the zero-sequence component is discarded using a Selector block because the grid-connected three-phase system operates under balanced conditions. Consequently, only the d-axis and q-axis components are supplied to the control loops. Since the PLL aligns the rotating reference frame with the grid voltage vector, the transformed d and q quantities become nearly constant under steady-state conditions. This conversion of sinusoidal three-phase signals into DC quantities significantly simplifies PI controller design and enables independent regulation of active and reactive power in the grid-connected inverter.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 522 0 R
/Next 456 0 R
>>
endobj
